content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow: the approximately 20% reduction over two weeks at unchanged valve settings is a documented low-flow/low-head symptom requiring troubleshooting. The HF-300 rated point is 300 m3/h at 45 m, but neither actual flow/head nor a minimum-flow alarm or trip limit is supplied; therefore the reading cannot be converted into an absolute flow or compared numerically with a documented flow limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 severity chart for velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported 2.0 mm/s is an RMS bearing-housing reading, it falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines') and is below the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary. It is not in the restricted Zone C or the stop-pump Zone D. The manual requires readings on both bearing housings and classification of the highest value, so confirmation of measurement basis and both-housing coverage is still required.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: using the documented bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, the reported 65 C is within the normal range of up to 70 C, below the 80 C alarm and below the 90 C trip. Confirm that 'housing' in the report means the bearing-housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage is reported. The troubleshooting table provides a leakage-at-shaft-seal diagnostic path but no numerical allowable leakage rate; the present report does not establish a leaking-seal failure or, by itself, justify seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: the supplied readings do not reach the documented bearing-temperature trip or vibration Zone D stop condition, so immediate shutdown is not supported. P2 planned investigation is a planning judgment based on the persistent approximately 20% loss of pump performance despite normal reported temperature and Zone A vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Worn impeller — investigate first because the manual identifies it as a probable cause of low flow or head, and the deterioration developed progressively while valve settings remained unchanged. Inspect the impeller and also the wear rings as directed by the corrective action.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Air in the suction — expressly listed as a probable cause of low flow or head; check for air and vent the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Closed or incorrectly positioned valve — also listed by the manual. Unchanged settings make this less compelling than the first two checks but do not verify actual valve position, so it remains a check rather than an excluded cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Record the current and available pre-fault flow, head and operating conditions at the unchanged valve settings. Verify actual valve positions, check for air in the suction and vent the casing. Do not assume that the 300 m3/h at 45 m rated point was the pump's pre-fault duty.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS and classify the highest reading with Figure 3. Record the bearing-housing surface temperature and compare it with the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip values. Retain these results as the pre-work baseline.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the initial checks do not restore flow, isolate and drain the pump before disassembly. Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; its design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. Remove the assembly as required and inspect the impeller and wear rings, recording their condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If impeller or wear-ring deterioration is found, hold the affected components for engineering disposition before replacement: the evidence directs inspection but supplies no impeller/wear-ring acceptance limits. The identified impeller spare is HF3-210, 5-vane, 330 mm, quantity 1; no wear-ring part number is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if mechanical-seal replacement is included in the approved scope, follow procedure 5.2: remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and fit a new seal and new casing gasket. For serial HF3-22300, fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450. No sleeve-setting measurement is needed for HF3-450B, but the scoring inspection still applies; replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "When reassembling disturbed fasteners, apply the Table 5 torques for lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. For the HF3-450B seal, tighten the M10 seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the generic 25 Nm value. Install a new casing gasket whenever the casing is opened and during mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not replace bearings solely on the present 2.0 mm/s and 65 C readings. If subsequent inspection finds bearing wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair and revise the work scope accordingly.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before running, maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. After the work, repeat flow/head, both-housing vibration and bearing-housing surface-temperature checks, classify the highest vibration reading, and inspect for shaft-seal leakage. Compare flow recovery with the established pre-fault duty rather than assuming the rated point is the site acceptance value.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-210",
      "description": "Impeller, 5-vane, 330 mm. Conditional replacement only if inspection identifies impeller wear as the cause; no wear limit is supplied.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. Conditional on mechanical-seal replacement being approved; required instead of HF3-450 for this serial range. gland torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Replace only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened and fit a new gasket during mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before beginning mechanical-seal disassembly or other intrusive work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During condition checks, stop the pump if the highest bearing-housing vibration is classified in Figure 3 Zone D, labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump' (documented range 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS). Zone C (4.5–7.1) is restricted and requires planned maintenance. The current 2.0 mm/s reading, if RMS, is not in either zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply the bearing-housing surface-temperature limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 65 C is below all three thresholds.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Initial low-flow troubleshooting and impeller/wear-ring inspection have no standard time in Table 6; their duration must be estimated after the inspection scope and findings are known.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal replacement is performed, the standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-pair replacement becomes necessary because of wear, noise or high temperature, the standard allowance is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians; both bearings are replaced together.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If laser alignment is required after movement of the motor or bearing housing, allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No fixed total work-order duration is calculated because seal replacement, bearing replacement and alignment are conditional scopes, and troubleshooting/impeller inspection has no tabulated standard time.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal selection: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and specifies HF3-450B. P-112 is serial HF3-22300, so the bulletin explicitly applies and HF3-450B governs over the generic manual parts-list entry if a seal is fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because P-112 is within the bulletin's serial range and any new seal must be HF3-450B, use 30 Nm for that seal. The other Table 5 fastener torques remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve instructions are complementary rather than grounds to omit inspection: HF3-450B needs no sleeve-setting measurement because it is pre-set, but procedure 5.2 still requires scoring inspection and the bulletin supplies the replacement criterion of scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth for this serial range.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What were the actual pre-fault and current flow and head, and what are the suction conditions and verified valve positions? The rated point alone does not establish the degraded duty or a flow acceptance limit (C02, C09).",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS, on which bearing housing was it taken, and what was the reading on the other housing? Was the 65 C temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface (C01, C02, C06, C07)?",
    "What are the impeller and wear-ring inspection/acceptance limits, the wear-ring part number, and the approved replacement procedure if wear is found? These are not supplied (C05, C09).",
    "Is mechanical-seal replacement actually required, or is the scope only low-flow troubleshooting and impeller inspection? No leakage is reported, and SB-2026-014 supersedes the replacement part but does not explicitly mandate proactive replacement of an installed non-leaking seal (C09, C13).",
    "What site production consequence and P1/P2/P3 priority definitions apply? P2 is a planning judgment because no site priority matrix or service-criticality information is included.",
    "What labour allowance and post-work performance acceptance criterion should apply to troubleshooting, impeller/wear-ring inspection and any impeller repair? Table 6 covers only seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment (C02, C09, C12)."
  ]
}
